IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `fhog-terms`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`
IMPORT `sda-home`

-- Stamp Duties Act 1923 (SA) -- cases for the home-conveyance core (sda-home.l4).
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (as at 2025-02-13): the Schedule 2 clause 3(1)(b)
-- scale and the s 72 surcharge were also done in an independent calculator written from the statutory words (scratchpad
-- au-sa-1/hand.py), never copied from this encoding's output. Dates were counted on a calendar. Regulative rules are
-- asserted with EVALTRACE where the trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it ends in a breach
-- or a pending obligation. Clock: days.
--
-- "The relevant day" is an INPUT. The cases use 13 February 2025, the assent date of the Statutes Amendment (Budget
-- Measures) Act 2025 (No 4 of 2025) as the deposited legislative history records it (NOTES.md, finding 3).
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (CC BY 4.0). Not the official text. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the buyer of a home`

`the relevant day used in the cases` MEANS YMD 2025 2 13

§§ `s 60A -- value of the property conveyed`

#ASSERT `the value of the property conveyed (s 60A)` 590000 600000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 600000
#ASSERT `the value of the property conveyed (s 60A)` 650000 600000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 650000
#ASSERT `the value of the property conveyed (s 60A)` 400000 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 400000

§§ `Schedule 2 clause 3(1)(b) -- the general scale`

-- Band (i): $1 per $100 or part.
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 5000 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 11999.50 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 12000 EQUALS 120
-- Band (ii): $120 plus $2 per $100 or part over $12 000; $50 over counts as a whole $100.
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 12050 EQUALS 122
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 25000 EQUALS 380
-- Each band's base is the duty at the top of the band below: the scale is continuous.
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 30000 EQUALS 480
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 40000 EQUALS 780
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 50000 EQUALS 1080
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 75000 EQUALS 1955
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 100000 EQUALS 2830
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 100001 EQUALS 2834
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 150000 EQUALS 4830
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 200000 EQUALS 6830
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 220000 EQUALS 7680
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 250000 EQUALS 8955
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 280000 EQUALS 10380
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 300000 EQUALS 11330
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 300050 EQUALS 11335
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 400000 EQUALS 16330
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 450000 EQUALS 18830
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 500000 EQUALS 21330
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 600000 EQUALS 26830
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 640000 EQUALS 29030
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 650000 EQUALS 29580
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 700000 EQUALS 32330
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty on the general scale` 1000000 EQUALS 48830

§§ `s 20 -- time for payment and stamping`

-- Executed in South Australia on 15 March 2026: two months after is 15 May 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day to pay the duty and stamp the instrument (s 20(1))` (YMD 2026 3 15) `in South Australia` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 15
-- READING: 31 December 2025 plus two months is 28 February 2026, the month having no 31st.
#ASSERT `the last day to pay the duty and stamp the instrument (s 20(1))` (YMD 2025 12 31) `in South Australia` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
-- Executed outside SA on 1 March 2026 and received on 10 June 2026: 10 August 2026 comes before 1 September 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day to pay the duty and stamp the instrument (s 20(1))` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`outside South Australia` (YMD 2026 6 10)) EQUALS YMD 2026 8 10
-- Received on 20 July 2026: six months after execution (1 September 2026) expires first.
#ASSERT `the last day to pay the duty and stamp the instrument (s 20(1))` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`outside South Australia` (YMD 2026 7 20)) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 1
-- s 20(2): duty chargeable because of a later event on 1 August 2026 is due by 1 October 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day to pay duty that becomes chargeable after execution (s 20(2))` (YMD 2026 8 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 1
-- s 20(4)-(6): the most the person who executed it can be fined.
#ASSERT `the most the person who executed it can be fined (s 20(4)-(6))` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the most the person who executed it can be fined (s 20(4)-(6))` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the most the person who executed it can be fined (s 20(4)-(6))` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the most the person who executed it can be fined (s 20(4)-(6))` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- The rule: 61 days from 15 March to 15 May 2026.
#ASSERT `the days from` (YMD 2026 3 15) `to` (`the last day to pay the duty and stamp the instrument (s 20(1))` (YMD 2026 3 15) `in South Australia`) EQUALS 61
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 20 -- pay the duty and have the instrument stamped within the period` TRUE 61) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person who executed the instrument` `pay the duty and have the instrument stamped` 45)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 20 -- pay the duty and have the instrument stamped within the period` TRUE 61) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person who executed the instrument` `pay the duty and have the instrument stamped` 61)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 20 -- pay the duty and have the instrument stamped within the period` FALSE 61) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the person who executed the instrument, "s 20(1), (4): ..." (paid on day 62)
#TRACE `s 20 -- pay the duty and have the instrument stamped within the period` TRUE 61 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person who executed the instrument` DOES `pay the duty and have the instrument stamped` AT 62

