#ASSERT NOT (`the vehicle application is exempt (s 71CB(2)(a)(ii), (b))` TRUE `former spouses or former domestic partners` FALSE)

§§ `s 2 and s 71DD(11) -- who counts as a spouse`

#ASSERT `the person counts as the applicant's spouse for s 71DD` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the person counts as the applicant's spouse for s 71DD` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person counts as the applicant's spouse for s 71DD` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person counts as the applicant's spouse for s 71DD` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `s 71DD -- a purchase, with the facts most cases share`

-- Individual purchasers, all 18 or older, at least one a citizen, none with earlier relief or earlier property, all
-- applying together, no replacement contract. The parameters are the facts that vary between cases.
GIVEN `bought`                 IS A `What is bought`
      `day`                    IS A DATE
      `value`                  IS A NUMBER
      `held property before`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `lived in it 6 months`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `New home purchase`
`a purchase` MEANS
    `New home purchase` WITH
        `what is bought`                                                                   IS `bought`
        `the date the contract was entered into`                                           IS `day`
        `the market value when the contract was entered into`                              IS `value`
        `every purchaser is at least 18, or the Commissioner so determines under s 71DD(6)` IS TRUE
        `at least one purchaser is an Australian citizen or permanent resident when applying` IS TRUE
        `a purchaser or spouse was a party to an earlier conveyance relieved under s 71DD(2)` IS FALSE
        `a purchaser or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in SA or another State before the contract` IS `held property before`
        `a purchaser or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months` IS `lived in it 6 months`
        `the relevant day`                                                                 IS `the relevant day used in the cases`
        `every applicant is a natural person`                                              IS TRUE
        `every owner after the transfer joins in the application`                          IS TRUE
        `the Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land` IS FALSE

-- A first home buyer of a new home in 2026 at $640 000: nil duty (s 71DD(2)(b)), instead of $29 030.
`the 2026 new home` MEANS `a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2026 9 1) 640000 FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` `the 2026 new home`
#ASSERT `s 71DD applies to the conveyance (s 71DD(1), (8), (9))` `the 2026 new home`
#ASSERT `the relief under s 71DD(2)` `the 2026 new home` EQUALS `no duty is payable`
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` `the 2026 new home` 29030 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0

-- From 6 June 2024 there is no value cap: a $1 000 000 new home pays nothing instead of $48 830.
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2026 9 1) 1000000 FALSE FALSE) 48830 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
-- Vacant land to build on, 2026, $480 000: nil instead of $20 330.
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `vacant land on which a home is to be built` (YMD 2026 9 1) 480000 FALSE FALSE) 20330 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0

-- s 71DD(3)(e): a contract on or after the relevant day is barred by having held a relevant interest, even one never
-- lived in.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2026 9 1) 640000 TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2026 9 1) 640000 TRUE FALSE) 29030 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 29030
-- A contract of 1 December 2024 (before the relevant day): a relevant interest never lived in for 6 months does not bar.
#ASSERT `the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 12 1) 640000 TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 12 1) 640000 TRUE TRUE))
-- The relevant day itself counts as "on or after" it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2025 2 13) 640000 TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2025 2 12) 640000 TRUE FALSE)

-- Before 6 June 2024: nil up to $650 000 (home) or $400 000 (land); in the phase-out band the s 71DD(7) formula is
-- missing, so `not covered`; at $700 000 or $450 000 and above, no relief (s 71DD(3)(f)).
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 1 10) 640000 FALSE FALSE) 29030 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 1 10) 650000 FALSE FALSE) 29580 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 1 10) 680000 FALSE FALSE) 31230 EQUALS `not covered` `the s 71DD(7) formula for the reduction on a pre-6 June 2024 contract in the phase-out band is missing from the deposited text`
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 1 10) 700000 FALSE FALSE) 32330 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 32330
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `vacant land on which a home is to be built` (YMD 2024 1 10) 380000 FALSE FALSE) 15330 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `vacant land on which a home is to be built` (YMD 2024 1 10) 420000 FALSE FALSE) 17330 EQUALS `not covered` `the s 71DD(7) formula for the reduction on a pre-6 June 2024 contract in the phase-out band is missing from the deposited text`
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`a purchase` `vacant land on which a home is to be built` (YMD 2024 1 10) 450000 FALSE FALSE) 18830 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 18830
-- 5 June 2024 is still before 6 June 2024; 6 June 2024 is nil at any value.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 6 5) 720000 FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the relief under s 71DD(2)` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 6 6) 720000 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no duty is payable`
-- A contract before 15 June 2023 has no relief.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2023 6 14) 500000 FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2023 6 15) 500000 FALSE FALSE)
-- An established home is not within s 71DD at all.
#ASSERT `the relief under s 71DD(2)` (`a purchase` `something else` (YMD 2026 9 1) 500000 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no relief: s 71DD does not apply`

-- The same 2026 purchase with one of the other criteria changed.
GIVEN `of age`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `a citizen`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `earlier relief`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `natural persons`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `all owners apply`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `a replacement`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `New home purchase`
`the 2026 new home, but` MEANS
    `New home purchase` WITH
        `what is bought`                                                                   IS `a new home`
        `the date the contract was entered into`                                           IS YMD 2026 9 1
        `the market value when the contract was entered into`                              IS 640000
        `every purchaser is at least 18, or the Commissioner so determines under s 71DD(6)` IS `of age`
        `at least one purchaser is an Australian citizen or permanent resident when applying` IS `a citizen`
        `a purchaser or spouse was a party to an earlier conveyance relieved under s 71DD(2)` IS `earlier relief`
        `a purchaser or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in SA or another State before the contract` IS FALSE
        `a purchaser or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months` IS FALSE
        `the relevant day`                                                                 IS `the relevant day used in the cases`
        `every applicant is a natural person`                                              IS `natural persons`
        `every owner after the transfer joins in the application`                          IS `all owners apply`
        `the Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land` IS `a replacement`

-- The other criteria, one at a time.
#ASSERT `s 71DD applies to the conveyance (s 71DD(1), (8), (9))` (`the 2026 new home, but` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`the 2026 new home, but` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`the 2026 new home, but` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` (`the 2026 new home, but` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 71DD applies to the conveyance (s 71DD(1), (8), (9))` (`the 2026 new home, but` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 71DD applies to the conveyance (s 71DD(1), (8), (9))` (`the 2026 new home, but` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 71DD applies to the conveyance (s 71DD(1), (8), (9))` (`the 2026 new home, but` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`the 2026 new home, but` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) 29030 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 29030

-- s 71DD(11a): the relief reaches the foreign ownership surcharge only on a contract before the relevant day.
#ASSERT `the s 71DD relief extends to the foreign ownership surcharge` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 12 1) 640000 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 71DD relief extends to the foreign ownership surcharge` `the 2026 new home`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 71DD relief extends to the foreign ownership surcharge` (`a purchase` `a new home` (YMD 2024 1 10) 680000 FALSE FALSE))

§§ `s 71DD(4), (5) -- the residence requirement`

-- A new home transferred on 1 August 2026: the residence period must begin by 1 August 2027.
#ASSERT `the last day to begin the residence period (s 71DD(4), (5))` `a new home` (YMD 2026 8 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 8 1) 0 EQUALS YMD 2027 8 1
-- The Commissioner approves a completion period of 18 months: 1 February 2028.
#ASSERT `the last day to begin the residence period (s 71DD(4), (5))` `a new home` (YMD 2026 8 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 8 1) 18 EQUALS YMD 2028 2 1
-- An approved period shorter than the statutory one does not shorten it.
#ASSERT `the last day to begin the residence period (s 71DD(4), (5))` `a new home` (YMD 2026 8 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 8 1) 6 EQUALS YMD 2027 8 1
-- Vacant land transferred on 1 August 2026, a home first lawfully usable on 15 March 2028: before 15 March 2029 (which
-- comes before 1 August 2029), so 14 March 2029 at the latest.
#ASSERT `the last day to begin the residence period (s 71DD(4), (5))` `vacant land on which a home is to be built` (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE (YMD 2028 3 15) 0 EQUALS YMD 2029 3 14
-- Home first usable on 1 December 2028: 36 months after the transfer (1 August 2029) comes first, so 31 July 2029.
#ASSERT `the last day to begin the residence period (s 71DD(4), (5))` `vacant land on which a home is to be built` (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE (YMD 2028 12 1) 0 EQUALS YMD 2029 7 31
-- No home usable yet: only the 36 months runs.
#ASSERT `the last day to begin the residence period (s 71DD(4), (5))` `vacant land on which a home is to be built` (YMD 2026 8 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 8 1) 0 EQUALS YMD 2029 7 31
-- Six months from moving in on 1 September 2026: 1 March 2027; a 3-month period approved: 1 December 2026.
#ASSERT `the day the residence period ends (s 71DD(4), (5))` (YMD 2026 9 1) 0 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
#ASSERT `the day the residence period ends (s 71DD(4), (5))` (YMD 2026 9 1) 3 EQUALS YMD 2026 12 1
#ASSERT `the day the residence period ends (s 71DD(4), (5))` (YMD 2026 9 1) 9 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1

-- The rule. Clock: days from the transfer on 1 August 2026: 365 days to 1 August 2027; a residence period of 181 days
-- (1 September 2026 to 1 March 2027); 61 days to pay after the relief ceases.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 71DD(4) -- occupy the home for 6 months, or lose the relief under s 71DE` `the purchasers` 365 181 61) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the purchasers` `begin to occupy the home as principal place of residence` 31), (WAITUNTIL 300)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 71DD(4) -- occupy the home for 6 months, or lose the relief under s 71DE` `a complying purchaser, the others exempted by the Commissioner` 365 181 61) 0 (LIST (EVENT `a complying purchaser, the others exempted by the Commissioner` `begin to occupy the home as principal place of residence` 31), (WAITUNTIL 300)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Never moved in: the relief ceases; the Commissioner advises and the duty is paid in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 71DD(4) -- occupy the home for 6 months, or lose the relief under s 71DE` `the purchasers` 365 181 61) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 366), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `advise the purchasers in writing that relief from duty is no longer available` 380), (EVENT `the purchasers` `pay the duty and have the instrument stamped` 420)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Moved in on day 31, out on day 120: the relief ceases from that day.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 71DD(4) -- occupy the home for 6 months, or lose the relief under s 71DE` `the purchasers` 365 181 61) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the purchasers` `begin to occupy the home as principal place of residence` 31), (EVENT `the purchasers` `cease to occupy the home as principal place of residence` 120), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `advise the purchasers in writing that relief from duty is no longer available` 130), (EVENT `the purchasers` `pay the duty and have the instrument stamped` 170)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the purchasers, "s 71DE(2)(e), s 20(2), (4): ..." (moved out on day 120, never paid)
#TRACE `s 71DD(4) -- occupy the home for 6 months, or lose the relief under s 71DE` `the purchasers` 365 181 61 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the purchasers` DOES `begin to occupy the home as principal place of residence` AT 31
    PARTY `the purchasers` DOES `cease to occupy the home as principal place of residence` AT 120
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `advise the purchasers in writing that relief from duty is no longer available` AT 130
    (WAITUNTIL 200)
-- expect: the Commissioner's written advice and the purchasers' payment, both pending (never moved in; day 366)
#TRACE `s 71DD(4) -- occupy the home for 6 months, or lose the relief under s 71DE` `the purchasers` 365 181 61 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 366)

§§ `s 71DE -- the duty and the interest and penalty tax when the relief ceases`

#ASSERT `the duty payable when the relief ceases (s 71DE(1), (2)(c), (d))` 640000 EQUALS 29030
#ASSERT `the duty payable when the relief ceases (s 71DE(1), (2)(c), (d))` 650000 EQUALS 29580
-- Not exercised: nothing.
#ASSERT `the most interest and penalty tax when the relief ceases (s 71DE(2)(f))` 29580 FALSE 200 4.1 `a tax default that is not deliberate` FALSE `no disclosure and no obstruction` EQUALS 0
-- Exercised: interest $29 580 x 12.1% x 200/365 = $1 961.19 (715 836/365), plus 25% penalty tax $7 395.
#ASSERT `the most interest and penalty tax when the relief ceases (s 71DE(2)(f))` 29580 TRUE 200 4.1 `a tax default that is not deliberate` FALSE `no disclosure and no obstruction` EQUALS (715836 DIVIDED BY 365) PLUS 7395
-- The Commissioner is satisfied reasonable care was taken: interest only.
#ASSERT `the most interest and penalty tax when the relief ceases (s 71DE(2)(f))` 29580 TRUE 200 4.1 `a tax default that is not deliberate` TRUE `no disclosure and no obstruction` EQUALS 715836 DIVIDED BY 365
-- Disclosed before any audit: 25% reduced by 80%, $1 479.
#ASSERT `the most interest and penalty tax when the relief ceases (s 71DE(2)(f))` 29580 TRUE 200 4.1 `a tax default that is not deliberate` FALSE `a sufficient disclosure while not subject to a tax audit` EQUALS (715836 DIVIDED BY 365) PLUS 1479

§§ `s 2(14) and s 72 -- the foreign ownership surcharge`

#ASSERT `the natural person is a foreign person (s 2(14)(a)(i))` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the natural person is a foreign person (s 2(14)(a)(i))` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the natural person is a foreign person (s 2(14)(a)(i))` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the natural person is a foreign person (s 2(14)(a)(i))` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- 7% of $600 000 is $42 000; of a half interest valued at $320 000, $22 400.
#ASSERT `the foreign ownership surcharge (s 72)` (YMD 2026 9 1) TRUE TRUE 600000 EQUALS 42000
#ASSERT `the foreign ownership surcharge (s 72)` (YMD 2026 9 1) TRUE TRUE 320000 EQUALS 22400
#ASSERT `the foreign ownership surcharge (s 72)` (YMD 2017 12 31) TRUE TRUE 600000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the foreign ownership surcharge (s 72)` (YMD 2018 1 1) TRUE TRUE 600000 EQUALS 42000
#ASSERT `the foreign ownership surcharge (s 72)` (YMD 2026 9 1) FALSE TRUE 600000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the foreign ownership surcharge (s 72)` (YMD 2026 9 1) TRUE FALSE 600000 EQUALS 0
-- s 72(5): a permanent visa granted on 1 May 2027, eleven months after acquiring on 1 June 2026, still holding: refund.
#ASSERT `the surcharge must be refunded on application (s 72(5))` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE
#ASSERT `the surcharge must be refunded on application (s 72(5))` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 6 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the surcharge must be refunded on application (s 72(5))` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 6 2) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the surcharge must be refunded on application (s 72(5))` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 5 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the surcharge must be refunded on application (s 72(5))` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE)
-- The refund as a rule.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 72(5) -- on application, the Commissioner must refund the surcharge` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person who paid the surcharge` `apply for a refund of the foreign ownership surcharge` 10), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `refund the foreign ownership surcharge` 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 72(5) -- on application, the Commissioner must refund the surcharge` FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Commissioner's refund, pending (applied on day 10)
#TRACE `s 72(5) -- on application, the Commissioner must refund the surcharge` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person who paid the surcharge` DOES `apply for a refund of the foreign ownership surcharge` AT 10
